MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The crimp connector assortment fits my repeated interest in keeping varied fasteners and repair supplies on hand, and the heat shrink tubing complements it by helping insulate wiring repairs.",
    "The gloves and super glue fit my adhesive and resin work: gloves help with messy handling, subject to chemical compatibility, while super glue serves quick repairs that mounting tape and casting resin do not."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Another infrared thermometer repeats a tool I recently interacted with without giving me a clear reason to need a second one; the decibel meter measures something I have no current need to check.",
    "The filament assumes I use a 3D printer, and the suction lifters assume a large-panel project that my history does not establish. The multimeter leads are potentially useful, but I cannot choose them confidently without knowing whether they fit my equipment."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in workshop tools seems to have been stretched into an interest in specialized equipment for projects I have not shown any sign of doing.",
    "My recent thermometer interaction seems to have been treated as a reason to want another similar thermometer, even though it may already cover that need."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of hardware assortments suggest I value supplies that cover several repair situations; a connector assortment fits that pattern better than supplies tied to unconfirmed equipment.",
    "Useful additions need to fill a gap in my existing supplies and fit the job or equipment involved. That makes quick-repair glue appealing, while test-lead compatibility and the tubing's single size affect whether I would choose them."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in practical repair supplies but assumed too much about specialized projects and my need for duplicate tools."
}
